<p>At the preceding checkpoint, the effort-7 search reduced the original photo from 6,220,181 to 6,183,475 bytes and the screenshot from 401,990 to 400,951 bytes. At that checkpoint, the screenshot was 2.442% larger than pinned jSquash. Its two remaining main lossless gaps were 2.049% for im26-2018 at effort 1 against wasm-vips and 0.294% for im26-1416 at effort 7 against jSquash. Every original sample remains exact in both independent decoders. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/lossless-dense-training-production-controls.json" download>Preceding replay controls</a> and <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/parity-funded-sampling-effort7-public.json" download>Earlier effort-7 results and source identities</a>.</p>
<p>Measured {raw.generated.slice(0,10)} on one Linux workstation. PureJsImage base revision <code>{raw.implementationRevision}</code>{raw.implementationDirty ? ' with local codec changes' : ''}. Codec source SHA-256: <code>{raw.implementationSourceSha256}</code>. These results measure a local repository build.</p>
<p>Additional fixture checks now cover multi-group global Palette and Squeeze streams, all 27 VarDCT transforms, grouped progressive alpha, and ordinary ICC and structured SDR conversion through 16-bit integer precision. Relative custom white points and primaries also convert to sRGB. Ordinary IEEE float input preserves source samples, converts supported ICC or structured SDR color to straight sRGB16, and supports explicit PQ/HLG/linear HDR conversion. Ordinary lossless output preserves binary32 samples and matching retained ICC profiles. Native Modular float and CMYK frames now compose before display conversion, including selected animation frames. Separate libjxl, LittleCMS and FFmpeg references pass in Node and three browsers. Further independent checks cover 24 mixed-alpha and wide-integer layouts, custom float fields, RGB LUT8/LUT16 XYZ profiles, relative custom HDR, integer ICC preservation, Float32 animation writing and selected HDR VarDCT frames. HLG and PQ forward writing support associated alpha and nondefault luminance targets. HDR VarDCT reference frames compose in linear color before the output transfer curve. Explicit lossy Float32 output uses Modular mantissa rounding with exact alpha. Independent native groups decode cropped bands. Remaining gaps include transformed implicit-palette prefix layouts, nonrelative custom color, wider ICC/CMYK profile families, wider integer VarDCT display, float VarDCT writing and progressive float-alpha or animation output. The runtime tables retain the earlier source, inputs and comparator versions. The current compression results above use a later repository build and preserve their separate source identity. These additional capability checks cover cases beyond that shared comparison cohort. See the <a href="https://github.com/a-r-d/PureJsImage/blob/main/jpegxl-codec-support.md">codec support checklist</a> for the supported scope.</p>
