<section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Correctness and API coverage</h2><p>Chromium main set: 16 still inputs, with 13 lossy decode fixtures. Counts retain failures. Encode counts include multiple settings. “Incorrect” means the declared exact-sample or RGB8 tolerance contract failed, not a claim that the library is generally broken.</p><div style="overflow:auto"><table><caption>Verified / attempted public workflows; all other outcomes retained</caption><thead><tr><th>Library</th><th>Operation</th><th>Verified / total</th><th>API absent</th><th>Unsupported</th><th>Incorrect</th><th>Execution failure</th><th>Unavailable / not tested</th></tr></thead><tbody>{summaries.map(r=>{const c=record(r.counts)?r.counts:{};return <tr><th>{names[subjects.indexOf(text(r.subject))]}</th><td>{text(r.operation)}</td><td>{n(c.verified)} / {Object.values(c).reduce<number>((sum,v)=>sum+n(v),0)}</td><td>{n(c['API not exposed'])}</td><td>{n(c['unsupported input'])}</td><td>{n(c['incorrect output'])}</td><td>{n(c['execution failure'])}</td><td>{n(c['environment unavailable'])} / {n(c['not tested'])}</td></tr>})}</tbody></table></div><details><summary>Native, animation, metadata and access probes</summary><div style="overflow:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>Library</th><th>Feature</th><th>Status</th><th>Scope / evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>{specialized.map(r=><tr><td>{text(r.subject)}</td><td>{text(r.feature)}</td><td>{text(r.status)}</td><td>{text(r.runtime)} · {text(r.sourceReport)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details><p>All four initialized in Node and Chromium, with representative Firefox and WebKit checks. Lossy animation in PureJsImage remains Experimental. Exact 3/5 ms timing is a separate edge case: wasm-vips normalizes it to 100/100 ms; its 30/50 ms control passes. Oxide timing fields did not match the expected timeline; its frame access and composition passed.</p></section>
<section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Current quality and compressed size</h2><p>{adequate.length} of {quality.length} PureJsImage/comparator/target comparisons have measured brackets no wider than 0.25 score points on both sides. The rest remain unresolved. The photo checkpoint freshly encoded 91 settings across four diagnostics at SSIMULACRA2 70/80/90 and retains Butteraugli coordinates, monotonicity evidence and missing intervals. Competitor curves retain their pinned versions and settings. Alpha is scored on black and white; comparator default alpha distortion remains visible. Exact graphic output does not substitute for a missing target bracket.</p><div style="overflow:auto"><table><caption>Current adequately matched size estimates; PureJsImage divided by comparator</caption><thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>SSIMULACRA2</th><th>Comparator</th><th>Size ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody>{adequate.map(r=><tr><td>{text(r.fixture)}</td><td>{n(r.target)}</td><td>{text(r.comparator)}</td><td>{n(r.ratio).toFixed(3)}×</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>These capped diagnostics do not establish original-size or HDR compression parity. <a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/quality-funded-sampling-public.json" download>All measured points, brackets and unresolved pairs</a>.</p><div class="jxl-tool-cards">{crops.entries.map(c=><figure><img src={c.path} width="256" height="192" alt={`Actual ${c.subject} crop from the earlier measured photo`} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{c.subject}{'score' in c ? ` · measured SSIMULACRA2 ${c.score.toFixed(3)}, setting ${c.setting}` : ' · normalized source'}</figcaption></figure>)}</div><p>Earlier comparison crops at identical 256 × 192 coordinates, shown without rescaling. They use actual nearby measured points rather than synthesized target-80 images and retain the earlier source. Source: {crops.author}, {crops.license}. <a href="/assets/jpegxl-comparison/provenance.json">Crop hashes and provenance</a>.</p><details><summary>Earlier paired lossless size and warm-time ratios</summary><table><thead><tr><th>Runtime / comparator</th><th>Scope / effort</th><th>Pairs</th><th>Median bytes ratio</th><th>Median warm-time ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows(raw.losslessPairs).filter(r=>rows(r.pairs).length).map(r=><tr><td>{text(r.runtime)} / {text(r.other)}</td><td>{text(r.scope)} / {n(r.effort)}</td><td>{rows(r.pairs).length}</td><td>{record(r.sizeRatio)?n(r.sizeRatio.median).toFixed(3):'unavailable'}</td><td>{record(r.warmTimeRatio)?n(r.warmTimeRatio.median).toFixed(3):'unavailable'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p>These retain the earlier source used for the speed measurements. PureJsImage divided by comparator, verified pairs only. Complete originals, capped diagnostics and precision fixtures stay separate. Equal effort numbers do not mean equal work.</p></details></section>
<section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Warm encoding and startup</h2><p>Representative capped photo, lossless effort 1, Node. Three warm operations after initialization, outputs materialized and independently checked. These are exact-output comparisons, not equal numeric lossy distances.</p><div class="timing-bars">{timings.filter(r=>r.status==='verified').map(r=>{const ms=record(r.warmMs)?n(r.warmMs.median):0;return <div><strong>{text(r.subject)}</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 720 32" role="img" aria-label={`${text(r.subject)} ${ms.toFixed(1)} milliseconds`}><rect width={Math.max(1,ms/maxWarm*720)} height="24" fill="#7e52b7"/></svg><span>{ms.toFixed(1)} ms {record(r.warmMs)?`[${n(r.warmMs.minimum).toFixed(1)}, ${n(r.warmMs.maximum).toFixed(1)}]`:''}</span></div>})}</div><p>Oxide exposes no encoding API, so it has no encoding time.</p><h3>Cold initialization plus first encode</h3><div style="overflow:auto"><table><caption>Same Node photo workflow; median [minimum, maximum], three fresh processes</caption><thead><tr><th>Library</th><th>Status</th><th>Cold milliseconds</th><th>Peak process RSS, MiB</th></tr></thead><tbody>{cold.map(r=><tr><td>{r.subject}</td><td>{r.status}</td><td>{r.time}</td><td>{r.memory}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Cold reports separately include initialization and first operation, with three fresh observations for selected cells. Process/worker harness startup and input fetching are excluded. Warm operations reuse initialized modules. Small differences on this interactive host are not durable wins.</p><p>Oxide's decoder returns PNG, so its measured workflow includes mandatory PNG export. No raw-decode speed ranking equates that workflow with the other outputs.</p></section>
<section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Startup assets</h2><p>Loaded encode/decode toolkit, required JS, WASM and worker assets counted once. Includes the common benchmark worker; these are not minimum decode-only application bundles. Brotli quality 11 is an offline estimate; actual requests used uncompressed no-store responses.</p>{footprints.map(r=><div class="asset-bar"><strong>{text(r.subject)}</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 600 28" role="img" aria-label={`${text(r.subject)} ${n(r.brotliBytes)} Brotli bytes`}><rect width={n(r.brotliBytes)/maxBytes*600} height="24" fill="#16858a"/></svg><span>{(n(r.brotliBytes)/1024).toFixed(1)} KiB Brotli · {(n(r.uniqueDeployedBytes)/1024).toFixed(1)} KiB raw</span></div>)}<p>wasm-vips uses concurrency(1), but still starts its pthread runtime and requires cross-origin isolation. Actual repeated worker-script transfers remain in the raw report. Native libjxl is an oracle only and never enters JavaScript runtime comparisons.</p></section>
<section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Preview I/O and memory</h2><p>PureJsImage's scaled region and oxide's full-frame PNG preview are different workflows; their latency is not ranked. The report retains first nonempty output, requested source bytes and transferred bytes. First-preview visual fidelity was not independently scored. <a href="/jpeg-xl/progressive/">Inspect actual stages in the local tool</a>.</p><div style="overflow:auto"><table><caption>First nonempty preview, Chromium, median [minimum, maximum]. Different outputs, no speed ranking.</caption><thead><tr><th>Library</th><th>Milliseconds</th><th>Transferred source bytes</th><th>Workflow</th></tr></thead><tbody>{previews.map(r=><tr><td>{r.subject}</td><td>{r.time}</td><td>{r.bytes}</td><td>{r.scope}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Node peak RSS is isolated per subject process and includes the runtime, prepared source, output, WASM and worker infrastructure. It is not encoder-managed storage. WASM linear memory was not separately instrumented. Browser memory is unavailable across the tested isolation combinations. Canvas memory was not measured.</p></section>
<section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Methodology, uncertainty and downloads</h2><p>Common inputs are pinned sRGB8 straight-alpha samples with orientation 1; high-depth samples are separate. Lossless validation includes color beneath zero alpha. PureJsImage's default lossy alpha must be exact; other wrappers' public lossy defaults may alter alpha, with that error retained. Native float probes and headroom 1/2/4 are not a perceptual HDR compression study.</p><p>Missing brackets, API boundaries, untested features and reference-limited comparisons remain visible. These inspected development sources are regression evidence, not an unseen holdout. The full comparison was rerun after the sample, ICC/HDR, animation and native crop updates. The dated library survey retains the pinned comparator versions.</p><ul><li><a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/website-data.json" download>Complete generated dataset</a></li><li><a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/REPORT.md" download>Methodology and reproduction commands</a></li><li><a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/subjects.json" download>Tested package manifests and hashes</a></li><li><a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/fixtures.json" download>Pinned input manifests</a></li><li><a href="/jpeg-xl/evidence/survey.json" download>Dated official-source survey and versions</a></li>{raw.sourceReports.map(r=><li><a href={`/jpeg-xl/evidence/${r.path.split('/').at(-1)}`} download>{r.path.split('/').at(-1)}</a> <small>SHA-256 {r.sha256}</small></li>)}</ul></section>
